E. Authentication and session
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓ E1 a user session cookie is httpOnly, sameSite and secure in production
  ✓ E2 a user session is a stored record, so logout revokes it server-side
  ✓ E3 login rotates the session token, closing session fixation
  ✓ E4 password verification does not distinguish an unknown email from a wrong password
  ? E5 admin session semantics are recorded as they are, not as one would wish — admin session is a stateless HMAC (max age 1000 * 60 * 60 * 24 * 7), so an individual token cannot be revoked; rotating ADMIN_SECRET invalidates all of them. Accept or schedule.
  ? E6 no default admin password ships, and an initialized deployment cannot be re-setup — verify by hand that no password hash is seeded in the shipped store

